## Success Criteria

Research is complete when:

- [ ] All sub-questions have been investigated
- [ ] Each agent has produced their findings file
- [ ] Insights have been shared between agents
- [ ] Final report synthesizes all findings
- [ ] Quality assurance checklist is complete
- [ ] All claims have sources
- [ ] No contradictions remain unresolved

---

## Important Notes

- **Avoid Duplication**: Each agent focuses on their assigned aspect
- **Stay Focused**: Don't let agents wander into other agents' territory
- **Document Everything**: Save all findings to designated files
- **Cross-Reference**: Link related findings between agents
- **Be Critical**: Evaluate source quality and credibility
- **Note Limitations**: Acknowledge what you couldn't find or verify

Begin by creating the decomposition file and assigning agents their research questions.